cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark or its corpus, please cite it as below."
title: "Vibe-Security Benchmark: Do Security Rules in the Prompt Prevent Vulnerabilities in AI-Generated Code?"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Hajibagheri
    given-names: Hadi
repository-code: "https://github.com/HajibagheriLabs/Vibe-Security-Benchmark"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-10-07
abstract: >-
  A pre-registered, blind-judged benchmark of the Web-Vibe-Security and App-Vibe-Security
  guardrails. Three open-weight models generated 717 artifacts for 60 web and mobile/desktop
  coding tasks, with and without the projects' AGENT_RULES.md in the system prompt. A calibrated
  three-judge LLM panel found the targeted vulnerability in 60.4% of baseline and 13.2% of
  guardrailed security-task outputs. The projects' Semgrep rules are also compared with
  Semgrep's public registry packs. Corpus digest (SHA-256):
  f401382a9ee87af1da415a3d076709bf3cd2100eb367cd55a79d3d7e950a6f91.
keywords:
  - AI-generated code
  - code security
  - LLM guardrails
  - vibe coding
  - static analysis
  - Semgrep
  - benchmark
